INSERT INTO modules (id,course_id,title,weight,sort) VALUES ('product-school-m0','product-school','Smart SIP Architectures & Step-Up Compounding',NULL,0) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET course_id=excluded.course_id,title=excluded.title,weight=excluded.weight,sort=excluded.sort;
INSERT INTO lessons (id,course_id,module_id,title,kind,body,minutes,published,sort) VALUES ('product-school-l0','product-school','product-school-m0','Step-Up SIP Mechanics & Wealth Multiplier','note','# Step-Up SIP Mechanics & Wealth Multiplier

*About 20 min*

## Overview
Step-Up SIP allows investors to automatically increase their SIP installment by a predefined percentage (e.g., 10%) or fixed sum (e.g., ₹1,000) every year in tandem with salary increments. This counters lifestyle inflation and supercharges terminal corpus growth.

## Key features
- Automatic annual indexation aligned with employee salary increments
- Cap threshold option (e.g. stop increasing once SIP reaches ₹50,000/month)
- Multiplies 20-year terminal corpus by up to 2.2x compared to a flat SIP
- Seamless bank mandate management without needing a new NACH every year

## Who it suits
Salaried professionals aged 24-45 with regular annual increments seeking aggressive retirement or milestone corpus building.

## Our advantage
FundsIndia was the pioneer of automated Step-Up SIPs in India. Our engine allows date-based, anniversary-based, or manual bump triggers with zero platform transaction fees.

## How to pitch it
Mr. Sharma, if you invest ₹10,000/month for 20 years at 12%, you will accumulate ~₹1 Crore. But if you simply step it up by 10% each year—matching your normal salary raise—your corpus becomes ₹2.25 Crores! You invest 2x more over time, but accumulate more than double the wealth with no extra effort.

## Client FAQs
**Q: Can the client modify or pause the Step-Up percentage later?**

Yes, FundsIndia allows one-click modification or capping of the step-up parameter without stopping the underlying SIP.

**Q: Does Step-Up require a higher initial bank mandate?**

We recommend registering an e-NACH mandate with a maximum debit limit (e.g. ₹1 Lakh) to accommodate future automated annual step-ups.',20,1,0) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET course_id=excluded.course_id,module_id=excluded.module_id,title=excluded.title,kind=excluded.kind,body=excluded.body,minutes=excluded.minutes,published=excluded.published,sort=excluded.sort;
INSERT INTO lessons (id,course_id,module_id,title,kind,body,minutes,published,sort) VALUES ('product-school-l1','product-school','product-school-m0','Flexi-SIP & Volatility Buying Trigger','note','# Flexi-SIP & Volatility Buying Trigger

*About 25 min*

## Overview
Flexi-SIP dynamically adjusts monthly investment amounts based on market valuation metrics (P/E ratio, 200-day moving average). When markets are undervalued, the system invests up to 3x the base amount; when valuations are stretched, it invests the minimum base.

## Key features
- Algorithmic valuation triggers without requiring manual market timing
- Higher allocation during market corrections for maximum unit accumulation
- Disciplined capital preservation during speculative bull market peaks
- Backed by FundsIndia proprietary research signals

## Who it suits
High-conviction investors with variable monthly surplus who want algorithmic market-valuation advantages.

## Our advantage
Proprietary quantitative valuation models calibrated over 15 years of market cycles, automated seamlessly via our smart order router.

## How to pitch it
Instead of trying to time the market yourself, Flexi-SIP acts as an automated institutional buying engine—buying aggressively when quality funds are on discount and maintaining disciplined pace when markets are pricey.

## Client FAQs
**Q: What happens if the client bank account has insufficient funds for a high trigger?**

The system defaults gracefully to the baseline scheduled SIP amount, avoiding mandate bounce charges.',25,1,1) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET course_id=excluded.course_id,module_id=excluded.module_id,title=excluded.title,kind=excluded.kind,body=excluded.body,minutes=excluded.minutes,published=excluded.published,sort=excluded.sort;
INSERT INTO modules (id,course_id,title,weight,sort) VALUES ('product-school-m1','product-school','FundsIndia Smart Investment Framework (SIF)',NULL,1) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET course_id=excluded.course_id,title=excluded.title,weight=excluded.weight,sort=excluded.sort;
INSERT INTO lessons (id,course_id,module_id,title,kind,body,minutes,published,sort) VALUES ('product-school-l2','product-school','product-school-m1','Three-Bucket Asset Allocation Architecture','note','# Three-Bucket Asset Allocation Architecture

*About 30 min*

## Overview
The Smart Investment Framework segregates capital into three distinct temporal buckets: Emergency/Liquidity (0-1 yr), Capital Preservation & Horizon Goals (1-5 yrs), and High-Alpha Compounding (5+ yrs).

## Key features
- De-risks investor psychology by securing short-term liquidity first
- Eliminates forced panic selling during bear markets
- Optimizes post-tax alpha using tax-efficient arbitrage and dynamic bond funds
- Dynamic Glide Path that shifts equity to debt as goals approach

## Who it suits
All retail and HNI clients planning for multi-stage goals: child education, home purchase, and retirement.

## Our advantage
Proprietary automated portfolio health check that monitors style drift, fund manager changes, and sector concentration across all folios.

## How to pitch it
We never treat your wealth as a single pool. By insulating your immediate needs in secure short-duration liquid buckets, your long-term equity engine can compound undisturbed through any market volatility.

## Client FAQs
**Q: How frequently does SIF trigger rebalancing notifications?**

Quarterly review notices are generated, with automated rebalancing prompts whenever asset class weights deviate by more than 5%.',30,1,2) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET course_id=excluded.course_id,module_id=excluded.module_id,title=excluded.title,kind=excluded.kind,body=excluded.body,minutes=excluded.minutes,published=excluded.published,sort=excluded.sort;
