INSERT INTO lessons (id,course_id,module_id,title,kind,body,minutes,published,sort) VALUES ('customer-support-l1','customer-support','customer-support-m1','e-NACH Mandate Rejection & SIP Auto-Debit Failure','note','# e-NACH Mandate Rejection & SIP Auto-Debit Failure

**Category:** Banking & Mandates - **SLA:** 12 hours

## When this applies
NPCI or destination bank returns rejection code for recurring e-Mandate registration (e.g., R08: Mandate rejected by customer bank, R03: Insufficient Funds, R10: Signature / Account closed).

## Common root causes
- Net banking credentials or debit card authentication timed out during NPCI Digio verification
- Bank account type mismatch (e.g., trying to set up mandate on a NRE/NRO or PPF account without proper permissions)
- Joint account requiring dual-signatory physical mandate rather than single digital e-sign
- Daily debit limit on client savings account lower than scheduled SIP installment

## Resolution steps
1. Pull NPCI mandate failure response from payment gateway dashboard.
1. If failure was due to technical gateway timeout, trigger automated 1-click re-authorization link to client.
1. If failure is bank limitation, check if client has alternate verified bank on FundsIndia (e.g. HDFC, ICICI, SBI).
1. Assist client to switch primary SIP mandate to alternate account or initiate physical NACH upload.
1. Ensure upcoming SIP schedule is adjusted to prevent double billing or late fees.

## Client message template
> Dear [Client Name], your recurring SIP mandate for [Scheme Name] of ₹[Amount] could not be activated by your bank due to [Reason]. Don''t worry—your investments remain safe and no charges have been deducted. Please tap here [Link] to instantly authenticate using Netbanking or UPI AutoPay in just 60 seconds.

## Escalation matrix
| Level | Contact | Timeframe |
|---|---|---|
| L1 Banking Operations | mandates@learninghub.support | 2 hours |
| L2 Payment Gateway Liaison | pg-ops@learninghub.support | 6 hours |
| L3 Banking Relations Head | banking@learninghub.support | 12 hours |',8,1,1) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET course_id=excluded.course_id,module_id=excluded.module_id,title=excluded.title,kind=excluded.kind,body=excluded.body,minutes=excluded.minutes,published=excluded.published,sort=excluded.sort;
INSERT INTO modules (id,course_id,title,weight,sort) VALUES ('customer-support-m2','customer-support','Redemptions & Settlements',NULL,2) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET course_id=excluded.course_id,title=excluded.title,weight=excluded.weight,sort=excluded.sort;
INSERT INTO lessons (id,course_id,module_id,title,kind,body,minutes,published,sort) VALUES ('customer-support-l2','customer-support','customer-support-m2','Mutual Fund Redemption Settlement & T+1/T+2 Payout Query','note','# Mutual Fund Redemption Settlement & T+1/T+2 Payout Query

**Category:** Redemptions & Settlements - **SLA:** 8 hours

## When this applies
Client redeemed units from Equity or Debt fund and funds have not hit bank account by expected time.

## Common root causes
- SEBI T+1 / T+2 settlement calendar difference due to state-specific bank holidays or non-business clearing days
- AMC cut-off time: Order submitted post 3:00 PM resulting in next business day NAV and cycle shift
- Bank account registered with AMC differs from primary FundsIndia disbursement bank
- Penny-drop verification pending on recently updated bank beneficiary

## Resolution steps
1. Fetch RTA (CAMS / KFintech) transaction order reference number and timestamp.
1. Verify order execution NAV date and exact SEBI settlement cycle (Liquid: T+1, Equity: T+2, International Feeder: T+3).
1. Query NEFT/RTGS UTR (Unique Transaction Reference) number from AMC disbursement log.
1. Provide client with AMC UTR number to enable rapid tracking with their receiving branch.

## Client message template
> Dear [Client Name], your redemption request of ₹[Amount] for [Scheme Name] was processed at NAV date [Date]. As per SEBI settlement guidelines, payout is scheduled for [Expected Date]. Your bank transfer UTR is [UTR Number]. The funds should reflect in your [Bank Name] account ending in [Last 4 Digits] by 4:00 PM today.

## Escalation matrix
| Level | Contact | Timeframe |
|---|---|---|
| L1 Settlement Desk | rta-settlement@learninghub.support | 2 hours |
| L2 AMC Relationship Desk | amc-liaison@learninghub.support | 4 hours |
| L3 Customer Grievance Officer | grievance@learninghub.support | 8 hours |',8,1,2) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET course_id=excluded.course_id,module_id=excluded.module_id,title=excluded.title,kind=excluded.kind,body=excluded.body,minutes=excluded.minutes,published=excluded.published,sort=excluded.sort;
