INSERT INTO courses (id,code,title,subtitle,category,description,level,hours,playlists,links,published,popular,sort) VALUES ('zoho-crm','ZOHO CRM','Zoho CRM','Daily CRM discipline','tools','How to use Zoho CRM for leads, follow-ups, deals, call notes and reports, with beginner video tutorials.','All sales & service',0,'[]','[{"title":"Zoho CRM Help Center","url":"https://help.zoho.com/portal/en/kb/crm"},{"title":"Zoho Academy","url":"https://www.zoho.com/academy/"}]',1,1,17) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET code=excluded.code,title=excluded.title,subtitle=excluded.subtitle,category=excluded.category,description=excluded.description,level=excluded.level,hours=excluded.hours,playlists=excluded.playlists,links=excluded.links,published=excluded.published,popular=excluded.popular,sort=excluded.sort;
INSERT INTO modules (id,course_id,title,weight,sort) VALUES ('zoho-crm-m0','zoho-crm','Zoho CRM essentials',NULL,0) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET course_id=excluded.course_id,title=excluded.title,weight=excluded.weight,sort=excluded.sort;
INSERT INTO lessons (id,course_id,module_id,title,kind,body,minutes,published,sort) VALUES ('zoho-crm-l0','zoho-crm','zoho-crm-m0','The Zoho CRM data model: Leads, Contacts, Accounts, Deals','note','# The Zoho CRM data model

Zoho CRM organises everything into **modules**. Knowing which module a record belongs in avoids duplicates and broken reports.

| Module | What it holds | Typical use for us |
|---|---|---|
| **Leads** | Someone who has shown interest but is not yet qualified | Website sign-ups, campaign responses, referrals |
| **Contacts** | A qualified person you actively serve | Onboarded or in-process clients |
| **Accounts** | A company / household | Corporate clients, family groupings |
| **Deals** | A potential sale moving through a pipeline | A lump-sum / SIP opportunity with amount and stage |
| **Tasks / Calls / Events** | Activities | Follow-up calls, review meetings |
| **Notes** | Free-text history on any record | Call summaries |

## Rules of thumb
1. **Search before you create.** Search phone number and e-mail first - duplicates split the client''s history.
2. **One owner per record.** The record owner is accountable for follow-up.
3. **Convert, don''t re-type.** When a lead qualifies, use **Convert** so history carries over to Contact/Deal.
4. **Log it or it did not happen.** Every call and promise belongs in the CRM, not in WhatsApp or your head.

> Confirm exact field names and mandatory fields with your team lead - they are configured per company.',10,1,0) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET course_id=excluded.course_id,module_id=excluded.module_id,title=excluded.title,kind=excluded.kind,body=excluded.body,minutes=excluded.minutes,published=excluded.published,sort=excluded.sort;
INSERT INTO lessons (id,course_id,module_id,title,kind,body,minutes,published,sort) VALUES ('zoho-crm-l1','zoho-crm','zoho-crm-m0','Working a lead: from first call to conversion','note','# Working a lead

## Daily routine
1. Open **Leads** -> filter *My open leads* -> sort by *Last activity* (oldest first).
2. Work **overdue Tasks** before new leads.
3. After every call: set the **disposition / status**, write a **call note**, and schedule the **next task**.

## A good call note (4 lines)
- **Situation** - who they are, goal, horizon (e.g. "35 y/o, wants Rs 50L for child education in 12 yrs").
- **Need** - what was asked / the concern raised.
- **Agreement** - what you told them and what they agreed to.
- **Next step** - what, who, and *when* (create the Task with a date).

## Lead statuses (typical)
*New -> Attempted to contact -> Contacted -> Qualified -> Converted* or *Not interested / Junk / Not reachable*.
Never leave a lead in "New" after you have called.

## Compliance reminders
- Do not promise returns. Quote only approved material.
- Record consent for communications (WhatsApp/e-mail) in the record.
- Do not store PAN/Aadhaar images in notes - use the approved document flow.',12,1,1) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET course_id=excluded.course_id,module_id=excluded.module_id,title=excluded.title,kind=excluded.kind,body=excluded.body,minutes=excluded.minutes,published=excluded.published,sort=excluded.sort;
INSERT INTO lessons (id,course_id,module_id,title,kind,body,minutes,published,sort) VALUES ('zoho-crm-l2','zoho-crm','zoho-crm-m0','Deals, pipeline stages and forecasting','note','# Deals and the pipeline

A **Deal** is an opportunity with an *amount*, *closing date* and *stage*.

## Keep the pipeline honest
- Move the stage only when the **exit criteria** are met (e.g. "KYC complete" before "Ready to invest").
- Update **amount** and **closing date** every time they change - forecasts are built from these.
- Use **Lost reason** when closing as lost; it is the most valuable data for improving the pitch.

## Views that save time
- **Kanban view** of the pipeline for stand-ups.
- **Custom views**: "Closing this week", "No activity in 7 days".
- **Reports/Dashboards**: conversion by source, calls per day, pipeline by owner.

## Weekly hygiene (15 minutes, every Friday)
1. Every open deal has a **next task**.
2. No deal has a **past closing date**.
3. Stale deals (>14 days no activity) are either re-engaged or closed.',8,1,2) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET course_id=excluded.course_id,module_id=excluded.module_id,title=excluded.title,kind=excluded.kind,body=excluded.body,minutes=excluded.minutes,published=excluded.published,sort=excluded.sort;
INSERT INTO lessons (id,course_id,module_id,title,kind,body,minutes,published,sort) VALUES ('zoho-crm-l3','zoho-crm','zoho-crm-m0','Templates, tasks, blueprints and automation (what to expect)','note','# Templates and automation

Zoho CRM can automate repetitive steps. Your admin configures these; you should know how they affect you.

- **Email / WhatsApp templates** - use only approved templates; placeholders (client name, scheme) are filled from the record, so keep the record clean.
- **Workflow rules** - e.g. auto-create a follow-up task when a lead moves to *Contacted*.
- **Blueprint** - forces a fixed process (you cannot skip steps) and may require notes or documents at a step.
- **Assignment rules** - new leads are routed to owners automatically.
- **Reminders** - tasks trigger notifications; clear them daily.

## If something looks wrong
Do not work around it. Raise it with your admin with: the record link, what you expected, what happened, and a screenshot.',8,1,3) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET course_id=excluded.course_id,module_id=excluded.module_id,title=excluded.title,kind=excluded.kind,body=excluded.body,minutes=excluded.minutes,published=excluded.published,sort=excluded.sort;
